  "observations": [
    "Four real journal observations across two channels retain the same original event and two original opposing witnesses; the resulting existing TellingLog has two rows, not four manufactured witnesses.",
    "A nanosecond observation cut excludes a later observed opposing witness despite its asserted earlier event time.",
    "The original journal exports four standards-admitted OTLP LogRecords in two channel batches.",
    "Conflicting same-source/id events remain recoverable as two complete journal messages, while the SignChain reading refuses atomically.",
    "Clock rollback preserves source causal order and complete custody; the explicitly time-ordered SignChain projection refuses instead of silently sorting history."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Temporary journal filesystem effects are tested locally. No network OTLP receiver, physical-durability guarantee or production process is asserted.",
    "SEAVT and SignChain use explicit current SignCell source links. Their declared released supplier versions remain unchanged pending verified publication.",
    "The cross-owner cases are additional integration qualification; they are not part of the package default unit suite or its published receiving enrollment.",
    "The runtime must select an explicitly appropriate clock reading before calling the ordered TellingLog projection on a source with backward observation clocks."
  ]
